HQ's third arm is answered and it is a refusal: integer MMQ under coopmat loses for BOTH types on
gfx1103, so the fix is the tile decode as briefed, not the routing. WI-1724 should be closed as
measured or re-scoped.

Two corrections to the lane's premises, both load-bearing:

- S-X8 mul_mm is FASTER than q8_0 at this shape (-6.8% after the fix, -4.7% before). The R48i 4B
  pp128 deficit is real but is not this shape's mul_mm; it stays open.
- The packed decode buys 2.2%, not the double-digit the VMEM accounting (16 -> 6 byte loads per
  8 weights, 8192 -> 3072 per BK step against 524,288 MACs) would predict if the decode were the
  ceiling. At this shape it is not; the coopmat tile schedule is.

Planted RED inside the SX8_PACKED_DECODE branch only (qh1 -> qh0, 4 of every 8 weights):
packed ON goes 16/17 with the new n=512 row FAIL at ERR 0.990118204 and the n=64 row 0/1, while all
