+# R52b — S-X8 under the coopmat `mul_mm`: the decode fix, and HQ's MMQ arm measured and refused
+
+Lane: lane-243. Branch: `lane-243/r52b-sx8-coopmat-mulmm-2026-09-15`.
+Inherited SHA: **`50b0e9f7f`** (arifi/main, "series: regen at the R48i tip + replay fix (553 entries)").
+Worktree `C:/ArifiLabs/cache/r52b-wt`. Maker: Opus 5, MEDIUM effort.
+Inherited finding: R52's, that integer MMQ registers **zero** pipelines in the coopmat arm for every
+quantised type, so S-X8 and q8_0 both run the coopmat `mul_mm` f16 path on the 780M.
+
+## 0. Verdict, three lines
+
+1. **HQ's third arm is answered and it is a REFUSAL.** Integer MMQ under coopmat is **1.55x slower
+   than the coopmat `mul_mm`** for S-X8 and **1.18x slower** for q8_0 at the prefill shape. The fix
+   is the tile decode, as briefed — **not** routing, and **not** WI-1724.
+2. **The decode fix lands: −2.20% dispatch time, arms non-overlapping** — smaller than the VMEM
+   accounting predicts, which is itself the finding: at this shape the decode is not the ceiling.
+3. **The brief's premise does not hold at this shape.** S-X8 `mul_mm` is **FASTER than q8_0** here
+   (57.4 ms vs 61.7 ms, −6.8%), before and after the fix. The R48i 4B pp128 deficit is real but its
+   cause is **not** the 27B-class prefill `mul_mm` shape; it is still open.
+
+## 1. The coverage hole found on the way in, which is why nothing measured this before
+
+**Every S-X8 `MUL_MAT` row in `test-backend-ops` was `n <= 8`.** `ggml_vk_mul_mat_q_f16` only reaches
+the `mul_mm` (matrix-matrix) path at wide `n`; below that it takes the mat-vec kernels. So the S-X8
+`mul_mm` tile decode — the thing WI-1722b shipped and this lane rewrites — had **no correctness case
+and no timing case at any width it actually runs at**, other than one `m=1, n=64, k=256` row.
+
+Added (`tests/test-backend-ops.cpp:10768-10777`): `m=17408, n=512, k=5120` for `SX8` **and** `Q8_0`,
+the 27B FFN row at one prefill chunk, with q8_0 as the paired control. Every number below is that row.
+
+The planted red proves the hole was real: with the plant live and packed decode ON, the `m=17408`
+S-X8 filter goes **16/17** — the ONE failing case is the new `n=512` row; all sixteen `n<=8` rows stay
+green because they never touch `mul_mm`.
+
+## 2. Mechanism, with file:line
+
+`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mm_funcs.glsl:155-198`, the `DATA_A_SX8` arm of
+`load_a_to_shmem()`. `LOAD_VEC_A` is pinned to 8 host-side (`vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp:727`), so one
+invocation owns one 8-weight sub-block. The shipped loop re-reads the planes **once per weight**:
+
+| | byte loads per 8 weights | VMEM ops per weight |
+|---|---|---|
+| `q8_0` (`mul_mm_funcs.glsl:141-154`) | 4 (two 16-bit loads per 4 weights) | **0.5** |
+| S-X8, shipped scalar arm | 8 `qh` + 8 `ql` = **16** | **2.0** |
+| S-X8, packed arm (this lane) | 4 `qh` + 2 `ql` = **6** | **0.75** |
+
+On a 128x32 A-tile that is **8192 -> 3072 byte loads per BK step**, feeding 524,288 MACs: the decode
+is 1/128 of the arithmetic. The fix reuses `sx8_levels4()` (`types.glsl:2135`), already in the tree
+since lane-230/R46 for the mat-vec — four weights from three byte reads, one level per byte lane.
+
+**Refused, with the reason.** The brief's shared-memory/occupancy hypothesis (36,864 / 43,008 B vs
+32,768 B) is `mul_mmq` **integer** tile arithmetic (`mul_mmq_shmem_types.glsl`), which R52 proved is
+dead on this device. `mul_mm`'s `buf_a` is an f16 float buffer sized by `(BM+BN)*(BK+pad)*type_size`
+— **type-independent**. S-X8 and q8_0 get the identical tile geometry here. Not a cycle was spent on it.
+
+## 3. The fix, and the switch
+
+| file:line | change |
+|---|---|
+| `mul_mm_funcs.glsl:155-198` | `SX8_PACKED_DECODE` arm: two `sx8_levels4()` calls + `unpack8`, four `store_a` of the same slots. `#else` keeps the shipped loop byte for byte. |
+| `vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp:733-741` | emits `matmul_sx8p_f32` as a second SPIR-V variant of `mul_mm.comp`. |
+| `ggml-vulkan.cpp:6215-6234` | `sx8_mm_packed` — RDNA3 device probe, `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MM_PACKED=0\|1` override, stderr receipt. |
+| `ggml-vulkan.cpp:6412-6417`, `:6582-6586`, `:6822-6826` | the `if (sx8_mm_packed)` pick, in **all three** arms of `ggml_vk_load_shaders` (coopmat, fp16, else). |
+
+Switch name: **`GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MM_PACKED`**. Device-probe default ON for AMD RDNA3.
+
+**A specialization constant was REFUSED and the reason is load-bearing.** `ggml_vk_mul_mm_spec`
+(`ggml-vulkan.cpp:6202`) builds the vector **positionally**: on a non-Intel device it ends at
+constantID 11 (`ALIGNED`) and 12/13 are absent. A 13th `push_back` would land on constantID **12 =
+`SHMEM_STRIDE_PAD`** and silently corrupt shared-memory striding for every `mul_mm` pipeline of every
+type. Two SPIR-V variants with a runtime pick is the fork's own `dot2_f16` shape and is type-scoped.
+
+### HQ's scope addition: `GGML_ARIFI_MMQ_UNDER_COOPMAT`, default OFF
+
+`ggml-vulkan.cpp:6236-6249` (switch) and `:6419-6440` (a `CREATE_MMQ` macro + the q8_0 and S-X8
+registrations inside the coopmat arm). **No routing code changed**: `mul_mmq.comp` is a scalar
+integer-dot shader, not a coopmat one, its SPIR-V is compiled and linked on every build regardless of
+device class, and `ggml_vk_get_mul_mat_mat_pipeline()` (`:9923-9929`) already routes on
+`pipeline_dequant_mul_mat_mat_q8_1[...]->is_empty()` alone. Registering the modules is the whole fix.
+
+## 4. The three-arm diagnostic — `m=17408, n=512, k=5120`, 3 interleaved rounds
+
+`GGML_VK_PERF_LOGGER` dispatch time on the single new test case, one binary, arms env-gated.
+Receipt `r52b-evidence/20-perf-3arm.txt`, rc=0.
+
+| arm | S-X8 (us, 3 rounds) | median | q8_0 (us) | median |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **A1** coopmat `mul_mm`, packed **OFF** (shipped) | 59204 / 58738 / 58279 | **58738** | — | — |
+| **A2** coopmat `mul_mm`, packed **ON** (this lane) | 57444 / 57224 / 57522 | **57444** | — | — |
+| **A0** coopmat `mul_mm` control | — | — | 63196 / 59694 / 61651 | **61651** |
+| **B** integer MMQ **under coopmat** | 89153 / 91391 / 90967 | **90967** | 72037 / 75823 / 72501 | **72501** |
+| **C** `GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT=1` | 91824 / 91616 / 92269 | **91824** | 72697 / 79281 / 73099 | **73099** |
+
+Reading:
+
+- **A2 vs A1 = −2.20%**, and the raw rounds are **non-overlapping**: `max(A2) 57522 < min(A1) 58279`.
+  Repeatable, not noise — but far under what 16 -> 6 byte loads per sub-block would buy if the decode
+  were the ceiling. **At this shape it is not**; the coopmat MFMA pipeline is.
+- **B loses, decisively, for BOTH types.** S-X8 90967 vs 58738 = **+54.9% time (1.55x slower)**; q8_0
+  72501 vs 61651 = **+17.6%**. Integer MMQ is not the missing win on gfx1103 at prefill width — it is
+  a loss, and a larger one for S-X8 than for q8_0.
+- **C ~ B for S-X8** (91824 vs 90967): with coopmat off the device takes MMQ anyway, so arms B and C
+  land in the same place. That is the cross-check that arm B really dispatched MMQ.
+- **The brief's premise fails here.** S-X8 `mul_mm` beats q8_0 at this shape by **4.7% before** and
+  **6.8% after** the fix. Whatever costs the 4B pp128 22%, it is not this shape's `mul_mm`.
+
+**Contention disclosure.** Another maker's `test-backend-ops` (pid 17472, 6.6 GB WS) was live
+throughout. The design is interleaved round-robin over one binary, so the load is shared by every
+arm; the A1/A2 gap is the only one small enough for that to matter and its rounds do not overlap.
+
+## 5. Correctness
+
+| receipt | run | result | rc |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `10-sx8-mulmat-packed-off.txt` | `test -o MUL_MAT -p "type_a=sx8"`, packed OFF | **109/109, 0 FAIL** | **0** |
+| `14a..14l` | the same 109 rows, packed **ON**, split by `m` into small invocations | **109/109 across the set, 0 FAIL** | **0** |
+| `15a/15b` | `m=17408` S-X8 and q8_0, `GGML_ARIFI_MMQ_UNDER_COOPMAT=1` | **17/17**, **9/9** | **0** |
+| `15c/15d` | the `n=64` rows, MMQ under coopmat | **1/1**, **1/1** | **0** |
+| `13-full-mulmat-default.txt` | full `-o MUL_MAT` sweep | **VOID — host `std::bad_alloc`** | −1073740791 |
+| `30-packed-decode-proof.txt` | helper vs `sx8_level()`, all 2^24 byte triples | `PACKED-DECODE-EXACT`, 0 mismatches | **0** |
+
+**The full sweep is OWED, and the reason is environmental, not the change.** Three attempts died with
+host `std::bad_alloc` at `MUL_MAT(m=5120,n=1,k=17408)` — a CPU-side reference allocation — while three
+other makers' sweeps held 6-16 GB each on a 31.7 GB one-pool box. The same row passes in isolation.
+The narrowed set above covers every S-X8 row the sweep contains, plus q8_0 under the new MMQ arm.
+`type_a=sx8,type_b=f16` rows report `not supported [CPU]` and always have; alone in a filter they make
+the harness report FAIL with zero cases run (`14g`), which is a filter artifact, not a regression.
+
+**Bit-tolerance.** The two arms call the same `sx8_range()`, produce the same levels (2^24 exhaustive
+check above), evaluate the same `rlo + step * level`, and write the same shmem slots — bit-identical
+**by construction**, so this is a scheduling change and no NMSE sweep is owed. Stated honestly: an
+element-wise device-side diff between the two arms was **not** run; 0 FAIL in both arms at the same
+5e-4 bound is the receipt that exists.
+
+## 6. Planted RED — in the NEW path, which is the whole point
+
+R52's lesson was that a plant in an undispatched path gives an identical observable. This one is
+inside the `SX8_PACKED_DECODE` branch only: `qh1` -> `qh0` in the `lv1` decode
+(`r52b-evidence/R52B-PLANTED-RED.patch`), corrupting 4 of every 8 weights.
+
+| run | arm | result | rc | receipt |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| plant live | packed **ON**, `m=17408` | **16/17 — `n=512` FAIL, `ERR 0.990118204 > 5e-4`** | 1 | `22a-red-packed-on.txt` |
+| plant live | packed **ON**, `m=1,n=64` | **0/1 FAIL** | 1 | `22b-red-packed-on-n64.txt` |
+| plant live | packed **OFF**, `m=17408` | **17/17 pass** | 0 | `22c-red-packed-off.txt` |
+| restored | packed **ON**, `m=17408` | **17/17 pass** | 0 | `23a-restored-packed-on.txt` |
+| restored | packed **ON**, `m=1,n=64` | **1/1 pass** | 0 | `23b-restored-packed-on-n64.txt` |
+
+Three things proven at once: the packed branch **is dispatched** at wide `n`, the switch **really
+selects** between two shaders (same binary, OFF arm green under the plant), and `mul_mm` is reached
+**only** at wide `n` (the sixteen `n<=8` rows stayed green with the plant live).
+
+Build log `09-build-red.log` shows ninja doing real work on the edited unit —
+`[5/9] Generate vulkan shaders for mul_mm.comp`, `[6/9] Building ... mul_mm.comp.cpp.obj`,
+`[8/9] Linking ... test-backend-ops.exe` — so the plant reached the binary, the discriminator R52
+had to close after the fact. Restored with `git checkout a63edc326 -- <file>`;
+`git diff a63edc326 -- ggml/` is **empty**.
+
+## 7. What HQ should do next
+
+1. **Close WI-1724 as a measured loss at prefill width**, or re-scope it: integer MMQ under coopmat is
+   1.55x slower for S-X8 and 1.18x slower for q8_0 on gfx1103. The switch stays in the tree, default
+   OFF, so the next person measures instead of assuming — in either direction.
+2. **Re-open the 4B pp128 deficit somewhere else.** S-X8 wins this `mul_mm` shape. Candidates not
+   covered here: `MUL_MAT_ID` (still f16-staging for S-X8 by design), the `n` band between 8 and 512,
+   and the 4B model's own row shapes.
+3. **The decode is no longer the S-X8 `mul_mm` ceiling** — 16 -> 6 byte loads per sub-block bought
+   2.2%. The next lever on this shape is the coopmat tile schedule, not the unpack.
+4. **Owed:** the full `-o MUL_MAT` sweep in a quiet window, and a serve-level A/B of
+   `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MM_PACKED`.
+
